    // arithmetic result with no Long operand, so keeping IT unboxed is what makes the
    // change affordable: an ordinary program allocates no box at all. The cost is
    // that a 64 bit value stays boxed even when it would fit in a double, because a
    // plain number means Int here - szNorm unboxes such a result, so kL boxes it
