    // Kotlin has no implicit numeric conversions, so the only value a declared type can
    // retype is an integer literal typed by its expectation - but that literal reaches a
    // property, a parameter and a return position exactly as often as it reaches a local,
    // and until now only the local carried the width. `class A { var y: Long = 1 }`
    // followed by `a.y * 1000000 * 1000000` answered -727379968 where java (JDK 24) on
