    // Int.MIN_VALUE and stays 32 bit. The equivalent Java program under `java` (JDK 24)
    // prints -2147483648 / 2147483647 / 0 for x, x - 1 and x * 2; without the fold this
    // grammar printed -2147483648 / -2147483649 / -4294967296, i.e. Long arithmetic.
    // Only the exact boundary TEXT is folded. up.in is the production's matched tokens
    // with the separators removed, so `- 2147483648` normalizes to the same string and
    // `-2147483648L` (a genuine Long) and `-(2147483648)` do not match at all.
    function kNegFold(t, raw) {
