    }

    // ================= Declarations: classes, interfaces, objects, enums =================
    //
    // A class is a DESCRIPTOR object: {__isclass, __name, __ctor, __parentSpecs,
    // __parents, __super, __secondary, __statics, __dataProps} plus one property per
    // method (so clsFind can walk it) and the mangled accessor entries get$x / set$x.
    // An instance is {__class: descriptor, <fields>} - plus __outer for an inner class
    // and __deleg for interface delegation. Method and accessor lookup walks the
    // descriptor and then its __parents (superclass first, then the interfaces), which
    // is how inheritance, interface default methods and `super.m()` all work.

