    // followed by `a.y = 1` used to store a plain Int, so `a.y * 1000000 * 1000000` gave
    // -727379968 where java (JDK 24) prints 1000000000000. Go's __ftypes table
    // (commit 457791c) is the same idea; the Kotlin version needs no zero-value builder
    // because a property always has an initializer thunk.
